{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SPD3000 guided hardware test\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy this file to `test_spd300.ipynb`, select the Python environment containing this checkout, and run the cells in order.\n",
    "The notebook imports the installed `siglent_spd3000` package, so its results exercise the actual driver implementation rather than a duplicate test script.\n",
    "Read-only cells come first, followed by direct hardware-control tests.\n",
    "The complete acceptance procedure remains in [`.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md`](.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Run this notebook only with the power supply isolated from sensitive hardware and connected only to a correctly rated dummy load or measurement instrument, so unexpected voltage, current, or output settings cannot damage anything.**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Keep the front panel accessible, and stop immediately if an output cannot be disabled.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Connection settings\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit the `connect()` arguments in this cell for the connection being tested.\n",
    "Replace `<TYPE>` with a `spd.ConnectionType` member such as `SOCKET`, `VXI11`, `VISA`, or `GATEWAY`, and replace `<IDENTIFIER>` with its matching address or resource.\n",
    "Use a power-supply hostname or IP address for `SOCKET` and `VXI11`, a complete enumerated VISA resource for `VISA`, or `localhost`/`host[:port]` for `GATEWAY`.\n",
    "The two commented connection-specific arguments explain when to enable them; leave both commented for raw socket, VXI-11, system-default VISA, or an unauthenticated local gateway."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "connection-settings"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import atexit\n",
    "from pprint import pprint\n",
    "from time import monotonic, sleep\n",
    "\n",
    "import siglent_spd3000 as spd\n",
    "\n",
    "if \"psu\" in globals():\n",
    "    psu.close()\n",
    "\n",
    "psu = spd.SPD3000.connect(\n",
    "    connection=spd.ConnectionType.<TYPE>,  # e.g., SOCKET, VXI11, VISA, GATEWAY\n",
    "    identifier=\"<IDENTIFIER>\",  # e.g., instrument IP, VISA resource, or gateway host[:port]\n",
    "    timeout_s=5.0,  # communication timeout in seconds\n",
    "    min_command_interval_ms=100.0,  # delay between instrument commands in milliseconds\n",
    "    verify_writes_globally=False,  # True adds readback after supported writes\n",
    "    # visa_backend=\"@py\",  # Uncomment only to force PyVISA-py for a VISA connection.\n",
    "    # token=spd.load_gateway_auth(\"gateway-auth.toml\"),  # Uncomment for an authenticated gateway.\n",
    ")\n",
    "atexit.register(psu.close)\n",
    "print(psu)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Identity, capabilities, and execution settings\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell performs fresh identity queries and prints the parsed model information, feature flags, timeout, and command interval."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "identity = psu.idn\n",
    "print(psu.idn); print()\n",
    "print(psu.capabilities); print()\n",
    "print(psu.settings); print()\n",
    "\n",
    "assert identity.model is psu.model\n",
    "assert identity.raw == psu.scpi.query(\"*IDN?\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Find a Python API from a manual SCPI command\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy a command line from the programming manual into `SCPI_COMMAND_FROM_MANUAL`; command arguments, capitalization, abbreviations, and a trailing `?` are accepted.\n",
    "`lookup_command()` prints the canonical `psu` path, read/write access, supported models, documentation source, and any friendly aliases without communicating with the instrument."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SCPI_COMMAND_FROM_MANUAL = \"MEASure:VOLTage? CH1\"\n",
    "matches = spd.lookup_command(SCPI_COMMAND_FROM_MANUAL)\n",
    "\n",
    "if matches:\n",
    "    print(f\"Python API matches for SCPI: {SCPI_COMMAND_FROM_MANUAL!r}\")\n",
    "    for match in matches:\n",
    "        print(match)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"No registered Python API matches SCPI: {SCPI_COMMAND_FROM_MANUAL!r}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Decoded system status\n",
    "\n",
    "`SYSTem:STATus?` is decoded into a typed immutable result containing the operating mode and CH1/CH2 regulation, output, timer, and waveform state."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "status = psu.system.status\n",
    "print(status)\n",
    "print(f\"System version: {psu.system.version}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. CH1 and CH2 read-only checks\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell compares programmed voltage/current properties with live measurements.\n",
    "Power is queried only on models that advertise that capability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for channel, source in ((spd.Channel.CH1, psu.ch1), (spd.Channel.CH2, psu.ch2)):\n",
    "    values = {\n",
    "        \"channel\": channel.value,\n",
    "        \"voltage_setpoint_v\": source.voltage,\n",
    "        \"current_setpoint_a\": source.current,\n",
    "        \"output\": source.output,\n",
    "        \"measured_voltage_v\": psu.measure.voltage(channel),\n",
    "        \"measured_current_a\": psu.measure.current(channel),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    if psu.capabilities.measure_power:\n",
    "        values[\"measured_power_w\"] = psu.measure.power(channel)\n",
    "    pprint(values, sort_dicts=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Basic CH1 output control\n",
    "\n",
    "These are three direct property writes without batching or automatic verification.\n",
    "Edit the literal values as needed; `psu.ch1.output = True` leaves CH1 enabled."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "psu.ch1.current = 0.1\n",
    "psu.ch1.output = True\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"CH1 set voltage: {psu.ch1.voltage} V, current: {psu.ch1.current} A, output: {psu.ch1.output}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "psu.ch1.voltage = 0\n",
    "psu.ch1.current = 0\n",
    "psu.ch1.output = False\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"CH1 set voltage: {psu.ch1.voltage} V, current: {psu.ch1.current} A, output: {psu.ch1.output}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Write verification\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell reapplies the current CH1 voltage, current, and output settings without changing their logical values.\n",
    "Inside `psu.verify_writes()`, each write is followed by its documented readback and raises `SPD3000VerificationError` if the returned value does not match."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "current_voltage = psu.ch1.voltage\n",
    "current_limit = psu.ch1.current\n",
    "current_output = psu.ch1.output\n",
    "\n",
    "with psu.verify_writes():\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = current_voltage\n",
    "    psu.ch1.current = current_limit\n",
    "    psu.ch1.output = current_output\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"CH1 voltage, current, and output writes were verified.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Batch execution\n",
    "\n",
    "Batch execution postpones I/O until the context or decorated function exits and sends the collected commands as one non-interleaved sequence.\n",
    "`responses` is an ordinary list that stays empty inside the block and is extended on successful exit with only explicit user-query results in source order; writes and automatic verification readbacks are omitted.\n",
    "Batching guarantees ordering and non-interleaving, not rollback."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.1 Context manager and responses\n",
    "\n",
    "Setters add writes, while property reads and query methods add parsed results to `responses` when the context exits.\n",
    "Because `responses` is a normal list, it supports indexing, iteration, slicing, and unpacking."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with psu.batch() as responses:\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "    psu.ch1.current = 0.1\n",
    "    psu.ch1.output = False\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.voltage\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.current\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.output\n",
    "\n",
    "print(type(responses))\n",
    "print(responses)\n",
    "ch1_voltage, ch1_current_limit, ch1_output = responses\n",
    "print(ch1_voltage, ch1_current_limit, ch1_output)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.2 Decorator\n",
    "\n",
    "`@psu.batch` uses the same batch context and resolves deferred values contained in the function's returned built-in containers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@psu.batch\n",
    "def configure_and_read():\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "    return psu.ch1.voltage, psu.measure.voltage(spd.Channel.CH1)\n",
    "\n",
    "ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage = configure_and_read()\n",
    "print(ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.3 Batch with write verification\n",
    "\n",
    "Combining `psu.batch()` with `psu.verify_writes()` keeps writes and their readbacks in one batch.\n",
    "The automatic readbacks perform verification but do not appear in `responses`; only the two explicit queries below are returned."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with psu.batch() as responses, psu.verify_writes():\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "    psu.ch1.current = 0.1\n",
    "    psu.ch1.output = False\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.voltage\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.current\n",
    "\n",
    "verified_voltage, verified_current_limit = responses\n",
    "print(verified_voltage, verified_current_limit)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@psu.batch\n",
    "def configure_and_read():\n",
    "    with psu.verify_writes():\n",
    "        psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    return psu.ch1.voltage, psu.measure.voltage(spd.Channel.CH1)\n",
    "\n",
    "ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage = configure_and_read()\n",
    "print(ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Repeated-query stability\n",
    "\n",
    "Repeated identity and status reads help reveal stale, truncated, or mistimed responses without changing hardware settings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "READ_ITERATIONS = 10\n",
    "started = monotonic()\n",
    "for iteration in range(1, READ_ITERATIONS + 1):\n",
    "    assert psu.idn.model is psu.model\n",
    "    current_status = psu.system.status\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"{iteration:03d}: status=0x{current_status.raw:04X}, \"\n",
    "        f\"mode={current_status.operating_mode.value}\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "print(f\"Completed {READ_ITERATIONS} iterations in {monotonic() - started:.2f} s\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Model-specific read-only checks\n",
    "\n",
    "Network settings and front-panel lock state are queried only when the detected model documents those queries.\n",
    "Some SPD3303X firmware/connection combinations do not answer the separately documented `*LOCK?` command; that optional check is reported without stopping the remaining tests."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if psu.capabilities.network:\n",
    "    print(psu.network.settings)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Network queries are not supported by {psu.model.value}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "LOCK_QUERY_RESPONDS = False\n",
    "if psu.capabilities.lock_query:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        print(f\"Front panel locked: {psu.locked}\")\n",
    "    except (spd.SPD3000TimeoutError, spd.SPD3000ProtocolError) as exc:\n",
    "        print(\n",
    "            f\"Warning: *LOCK? is documented for {psu.model.value} but did not return a usable \"\n",
    "            f\"response on this connection ({exc}). Later lock-state assertions will be skipped; \"\n",
    "            \"verify lock and unlock at the front panel.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        LOCK_QUERY_RESPONDS = True\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Lock-state query is not supported by {psu.model.value}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Read-only semantic and raw batches\n",
    "\n",
    "The semantic batch returns ordinary parsed Python objects, while the raw batch returns SCPI strings aligned with its commands.\n",
    "Both paths submit their two queries as one non-interleaved batch, which is especially important when the gateway is serving multiple clients."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with psu.batch() as semantic_responses:\n",
    "    _ = psu.idn\n",
    "    _ = psu.system.status\n",
    "\n",
    "batch_identity, batch_status = semantic_responses\n",
    "print(batch_identity)\n",
    "print(batch_status)\n",
    "assert batch_identity.model is psu.model\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_batch = psu.scpi.execute([spd.Query(\"*IDN?\"), spd.Query(\"SYST:STAT?\")])\n",
    "print(raw_batch.values)\n",
    "assert len(raw_batch.values) == 2\n",
    "assert all(isinstance(value, str) for value in raw_batch.values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Optional error-queue read\n",
    "\n",
    "Reading `psu.system.error` removes one entry from the instrument error queue, so this diagnostic is opt-in even though it sends no write command."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "READ_ONE_ERROR_QUEUE_ENTRY = False\n",
    "if READ_ONE_ERROR_QUEUE_ENTRY:\n",
    "    print(psu.system.error)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set READ_ONE_ERROR_QUEUE_ENTRY = True to consume one entry\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 13. Optional CH3 output test\n",
    "\n",
    "CH3 has no documented remote output-state query, so this test requires physical observation and always sends `OFF` in `finally`.\n",
    "Run it only with CH3 unloaded or connected to a correctly rated verification instrument."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_CH3_OUTPUT_TEST = False\n",
    "CH3_ON_SECONDS = 1.0\n",
    "if not RUN_CH3_OUTPUT_TEST:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set RUN_CH3_OUTPUT_TEST = True after preparing CH3 safely\")\n",
    "elif input(\"Type 'ENERGIZE CH3' to proceed: \").strip() != \"ENERGIZE CH3\":\n",
    "    print(\"Cancelled before sending any CH3 command.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        psu.output(spd.Channel.CH3, spd.OutputState.ON)\n",
    "        sleep(CH3_ON_SECONDS)\n",
    "        print(\"Confirm the CH3 front-panel indication and physical voltage now.\")\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        psu.output(spd.Channel.CH3, spd.OutputState.OFF)\n",
    "        print(\"Sent CH3 OFF.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 14. Optional timer and waveform configuration round trip\n",
    "\n",
    "This test is available only on SPD3303X/X-E, overwrites one timer group and toggles one waveform-display state after confirmation, verifies both, and restores their original values in `finally`.\n",
    "It deliberately does not start the timer or energize an output."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_TIMER_WAVEFORM_TEST = False\n",
    "TIMER_CHANNEL = spd.Channel.CH1\n",
    "TIMER_GROUP = 5\n",
    "TIMER_STEP = {\"voltage_v\": 1.0, \"current_a\": 0.1, \"duration_s\": 1.0}\n",
    "if not psu.capabilities.timer:\n",
    "    print(f\"Timer commands are not supported by {psu.model.value}\")\n",
    "elif not RUN_TIMER_WAVEFORM_TEST:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set RUN_TIMER_WAVEFORM_TEST = True to prepare this test\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    original_timer_step = psu.timer.set(TIMER_CHANNEL, TIMER_GROUP)\n",
    "    timer_status = psu.system.status\n",
    "    channel_status = timer_status.ch1 if TIMER_CHANNEL is spd.Channel.CH1 else timer_status.ch2\n",
    "    original_waveform = channel_status.waveform\n",
    "    pprint(\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"current_timer_step\": original_timer_step,\n",
    "            \"planned_timer_step\": TIMER_STEP,\n",
    "            \"current_waveform_display\": original_waveform,\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        sort_dicts=False,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    phrase = f\"OVERWRITE TIMER {TIMER_CHANNEL.value} {TIMER_GROUP}\"\n",
    "    if input(f\"Type {phrase!r} to proceed: \").strip() != phrase:\n",
    "        print(\"Cancelled before writing the timer group.\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            with psu.batch(), psu.verify_writes():\n",
    "                psu.timer.set(TIMER_CHANNEL, TIMER_GROUP, **TIMER_STEP)\n",
    "                if original_waveform is not None:\n",
    "                    changed_waveform = not original_waveform\n",
    "                    psu.output.wave(\n",
    "                        TIMER_CHANNEL,\n",
    "                        spd.WaveformState.ON if changed_waveform else spd.WaveformState.OFF,\n",
    "                    )\n",
    "            print(\"Timer and waveform configuration round trip passed.\")\n",
    "        finally:\n",
    "            with psu.batch():\n",
    "                if original_waveform is not None:\n",
    "                    psu.output.wave(\n",
    "                        TIMER_CHANNEL,\n",
    "                        spd.WaveformState.ON if original_waveform else spd.WaveformState.OFF,\n",
    "                    )\n",
    "                psu.timer.set(TIMER_CHANNEL, TIMER_GROUP, **original_timer_step)\n",
    "            print(\"Restored the original timer group and waveform-display state.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 15. Optional front-panel lock round trip\n",
    "\n",
    "This test locks the front panel only after confirmation and always sends `*UNLOCK` in `finally`.\n",
    "Programmatic state assertions run only if `*LOCK?` returned a usable response in the earlier read-only check; otherwise confirm both operations physically at the front panel."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_FRONT_PANEL_LOCK_TEST = False\n",
    "if not RUN_FRONT_PANEL_LOCK_TEST:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set RUN_FRONT_PANEL_LOCK_TEST = True to prepare the lock test\")\n",
    "elif input(\"Type 'LOCK FRONT PANEL' to proceed: \").strip() != \"LOCK FRONT PANEL\":\n",
    "    print(\"Cancelled before locking the front panel.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        psu.lock()\n",
    "        if LOCK_QUERY_RESPONDS:\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                assert psu.locked is True\n",
    "            except (spd.SPD3000TimeoutError, spd.SPD3000ProtocolError) as exc:\n",
    "                LOCK_QUERY_RESPONDS = False\n",
    "                print(f\"Warning: *LOCK? stopped responding ({exc}); verify the lock physically.\")\n",
    "        print(\"Confirm that the front-panel controls are locked.\")\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        psu.unlock()\n",
    "        if LOCK_QUERY_RESPONDS:\n",
    "            assert psu.locked is False\n",
    "        print(\"Sent *UNLOCK; confirm that the front-panel controls work again.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 16. Tests intentionally left to the acceptance checklist\n",
    "\n",
    "Tracking modes require verified series or parallel wiring, save/recall overwrites persistent setup memory, network writes can disconnect the instrument, invalid raw commands deliberately alter the error queue, and forced link failures require external intervention.\n",
    "Run those cases manually from [`.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md`](.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md) rather than turning them into casual notebook cells."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 17. Close the connection\n",
    "\n",
    "Run this final cell even after read-only testing so another process can immediately acquire the instrument."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "psu.close()\n",
    "atexit.unregister(psu.close)\n",
    "print(\"Connection closed.\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
